1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,162
Chapter three.

2
00:00:01,162 --> 00:00:02,392
Motion and magic.

3
00:00:02,392 --> 00:00:04,850
Turning websites into experiences.

4
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:08,791
A website is no longer just a collection of pages.

5
00:00:08,791 --> 00:00:14,605
Modern websites behave like films, games, interactive installations and digital worlds.

6
00:00:14,605 --> 00:00:16,342
Movement guides attention.

7
00:00:16,342 --> 00:00:18,013
Movement creates emotion.

8
00:00:18,013 --> 00:00:19,550
Movement tells a story.

9
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:23,280
Before the tools, learn the vocabulary.

10
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:26,338
A transition is a change between two states.

11
00:00:26,338 --> 00:00:30,438
A hover is an interaction when a cursor lands on something.

12
00:00:30,438 --> 00:00:35,511
Micro-interactions are tiny animations that make an interface feel alive.

13
00:00:35,511 --> 00:00:38,430
And easing is the personality of movement.

14
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:42,323
Easing is the personality of movement.

15
00:00:42,323 --> 00:00:44,194
Linear is constant speed.

16
00:00:44,194 --> 00:00:45,017
Mechanical.

17
00:00:45,017 --> 00:00:47,935
Ease-in starts slowly, building energy.

18
00:00:47,935 --> 00:00:49,956
Ease-out slows down gently.

19
00:00:49,956 --> 00:00:50,554
Natural.

20
00:00:50,554 --> 00:00:54,520
And spring feels physical, like an object has weight.

21
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:00,815
GSAP, the GreenSock Animation Platform, is the Hollywood camera crew of websites.

22
00:01:00,815 --> 00:01:05,773
It controls position, scale, rotation, opacity, colour, timing and sequences.

23
00:01:05,773 --> 00:01:07,640
One hero section, five moves.

24
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:08,799
The logo fades in.

25
00:01:08,799 --> 00:01:09,764
Text slides up.

26
00:01:09,764 --> 00:01:11,310
The image zooms forward.

27
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:12,404
Particles appear.

28
00:01:12,404 --> 00:01:13,563
The button pulses.

29
00:01:13,563 --> 00:01:14,400
One timeline.

30
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:15,985
Anime.

31
00:01:15,985 --> 00:01:24,015
js is lighter than GSAP, a beautifully animated short film, perfect for logos, menus and cards appearing one by one.

32
00:01:24,015 --> 00:01:26,300
Framer Motion is built for React.

33
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,830
A card enters from below, fading in and scaling up.

34
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:33,430
Perfect for page transitions, modals and dashboards.

35
00:01:34,570 --> 00:01:38,819
Lottie exports After Effects animations as JSON files.

36
00:01:38,819 --> 00:01:42,517
Perfect for mascots, loading screens and icons.

37
00:01:42,517 --> 00:01:44,798
It says: play this animation.

38
00:01:44,798 --> 00:01:47,237
Rive is its interactive cousin.

39
00:01:47,237 --> 00:01:49,519
It says: respond to the user.

40
00:01:49,519 --> 00:01:52,430
A character reacts when you click it.

41
00:01:53,510 --> 00:01:56,860
Smooth scrolling makes a website feel expensive.

42
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:58,534
Default scrolling jumps.

43
00:01:58,534 --> 00:02:04,466
Premium sites glide, with tools like Lenis, Locomotive Scroll and GSAP ScrollTrigger.

44
00:02:04,466 --> 00:02:05,861
Parallax adds depth.

45
00:02:05,861 --> 00:02:07,676
The background moves slow.

46
00:02:07,676 --> 00:02:09,490
The foreground moves fast.

47
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:13,839
ScrollTrigger connects animation to scrolling.

48
00:02:13,839 --> 00:02:16,210
At zero percent, the hero appears.

49
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:18,512
At twenty-five, the text reveals.

50
00:02:18,512 --> 00:02:20,605
At fifty, the product rotates.

51
00:02:20,605 --> 00:02:23,883
At seventy-five, the feature section activates.

52
00:02:23,883 --> 00:02:26,882
At one hundred, the call to action appears.

53
00:02:26,882 --> 00:02:30,370
This is how many award-winning websites are built.

54
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:33,685
There are three levels of animation.

55
00:02:33,685 --> 00:02:38,511
Level one is functional: useful movement, like buttons, menus and loading states.

56
00:02:38,511 --> 00:02:43,873
Level two is premium, adding personality: smooth transitions, hover effects, page reveals.

57
00:02:43,873 --> 00:02:48,460
Level three is cinematic: storytelling scroll, 3D scenes, interactive worlds.

58
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:51,579
Creative director translation.

59
00:02:51,579 --> 00:02:52,908
GSAP ScrollTrigger?

60
00:02:52,908 --> 00:02:56,265
Make scrolling behave like a cinematic sequence.

61
00:02:56,265 --> 00:02:57,245
Framer Motion?

62
00:02:57,245 --> 00:02:59,693
Add beautiful React-based movement.

63
00:02:59,693 --> 00:03:01,022
Micro-interactions?

64
00:03:01,022 --> 00:03:04,520
Add tiny moments that make the product feel alive.

65
00:03:05,510 --> 00:03:07,039
The NagaVision rule.

66
00:03:07,039 --> 00:03:08,798
A good website informs.

67
00:03:08,798 --> 00:03:10,709
A great website performs.

68
00:03:10,709 --> 00:03:18,432
The future belongs to experiences that combine design, motion, sound, interaction, A I, 3D and story.

69
00:03:18,432 --> 00:03:21,490
Next up, Chapter 4: the third dimension.
